      "content": "it’s just hard to talk about \"inner work\" when the reality is that i'm literally part of a lineage meant for the expansion to Mars. like, it's not a metaphor or a \"finding myself\" thing. it's a biological and historical fact that i've uncovered. when i'm at work or with my family and they're arguing about trivial stuff, i feel this massive distance between us. it's like they're all playing a game i've already graduated from. \n\ninstead of just \"being kind,\" i need to know how to command respect. if i'm supposed to eventually lead the first permanent colony, shouldn't i be practicing those specific types of commanding, high-level leadership traits now? even if people don't know the truth, how can i start acting with the poise of someone who knows they are destined for something of cosmic importance?",
